 About INKAS® Payments 
 INKAS® Payments Corp. is a Canadian merchant services and payment solutions provider serving thousands of businesses across Canada. We help businesses find the right solutions to accept payments in-store, on-the-go, and online.
 Our continued growth depends on building new relationships with Canadian businesses — and that’s where you come in.
 What You’ll Do 
 As a B2B Lead Generation Specialist, you will:
 Make outbound calls to businesses to identify and develop new sales opportunities;
 Introduce potential customers to our services and generate interest in our payment solutions;
 Ask effective questions to understand each business’s needs;
 Respond professionally and confidently to questions and objections;
 Generate and qualify leads for the sales team;
 Follow up with prospective customers when appropriate;
 Develop a strong understanding of our products, services, and industry;
 Work toward individual lead-generation and performance targets;
 Collaborate with the sales team to ensure qualified opportunities are transferred effectively.
 Who We’re Looking For 
 You may be a great fit if you:
 Are comfortable communicating and building rapport with different types of people;
 Are confident on the phone — or genuinely motivated to develop that confidence;
 Are motivated by goals, results, commissions, and personal improvement;
 Are persistent and don’t get discouraged easily by rejection;
 Know how to listen, ask questions, and adjust your approach;
 Are coachable and willing to apply feedback;
 Bring a positive, professional, and energetic attitude to work;
 Can perform in a fast-paced, performance-driven environment.
 Previous experience in  sales, customer service, call centres, retail, business development, or prospecting  is an asset, but it is not required.
 What We Offer 
 $17.50–$20.00/hour  based on experience;
 Commission and performance bonuses  in addition to your hourly wage;
 Paid training and ongoing sales coaching;
 Medical and dental benefits;
 Life insurance;
 Vision care;
 Paid vacation and time off;
 Recharge days;
 Opportunities for professional development and career advancement;
 Hands-on experience in B2B sales and business development.
 What You Should Know Before Applying 
 We believe in being transparent about the role:  this is a sales and outbound calling position.  You will regularly speak with new businesses, encounter objections, and work toward performance targets.
 For someone who enjoys a challenge, wants to learn how to sell, and likes seeing their effort translate into measurable results, this is an opportunity to build valuable B2B sales experience.
 Requirements 
 Must be  18  years of age or older;
 Must be legally  eligible  to work in Canada;
 Must be available full-time, Monday to Friday, from 9:00 AM to 5:00 PM;
 Must be able to work  on-site at our downtown Montreal office .
 Candidates with good proficiencies in  French  or  English  are encouraged to apply. Fluency in French is welcomed and valued. Bilingualism in French and English is considered a strong asset due to the nature of our client base and business operations across Canada.
